Changes in this copy: input may be in any language, not only Chinese; the answer is a JSON object
with "rewritten_prompt" and "wh_ratio" instead of the bare caption, with rules for escaping quoted
text and line breaks inside it; the model chooses the aspect ratio from a fixed list when the
request gives none; rules were added for the node's keep-words note, explicit line breaks in
multi-line text, and requests naming an artist or art medium; the text rules ask for alignment,
spacing and reading order, and the length targets were lowered to match the long-caption lengths
in the MOSS-Image technical report (arXiv 2610.23374, Table 7); a rule keeps watermarks, borders
and image defects out of captions, since the model was trained on captions that describe them;
the reference-image and bounding-box sections were removed (this prompt is for text-to-image
without layout boxes). The rest of the wording is unchanged.
